+import Contracts.Token.TransferMeets
+import Contracts.Token.Spec.ExportCollide
+
+/-!
+# Token: a specification that needs a keccak256 collision is refuted under the keccak256 model
+
+The negative control of the keccak256 model (Verify/Spec/KeccakModel.lean, docs/KECCAK_MODEL.md).
+`Spec/ExportCollide.lean` is solar-verify's export of `scripts/verify/keccak/TokenSpecCollide.sol`,
+Token with one clause changed: `msg.sender != to ==> balanceOf[to] == old(balanceOf[msg.sender]) + amount`.
+It holds of a run only if the recipient's slot is the sender's, so a proof of it would need a
+collision of keccak256 on `balanceOf`'s slots.
+
+* `transfer_meets` (TransferMeets.lean): the real spec of `transfer` holds of the erased tree under
+  `SlotsSeparated 0`, which `KeccakModel (mapSlots [0])` gives (`transfer_meets_of_model`).
+* `collide_not_meets`: under the same model the collision spec fails: `transfer(1, 0)` from a
+  storage where only the caller's balance is 5 leaves `balanceOf[1]` at 0, and the spec asks for 5.
