new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b5f6562
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/KECCAK_MODEL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,136 @@
+# The keccak256 model
+
+Solidity places every dynamic storage item at a keccak256 image: `m[k]` of a mapping at slot `p` at
+`keccak256(k . p)`, `n[a][b]` of a mapping of mappings at `keccak256(b . keccak256(a . n))`, array
+elements and struct fields at `keccak256(...) + i`. A proof about such code has to know that these
+slots do not collide with each other or with the small slots of scalar state variables. Keccak-256
+is not injective (it maps every input length onto 2^256 words), so this cannot be proved. It has to
+be assumed, and the assumption has to be stated, named and checked for vacuity.
+
+solidity-lean states it once, as the premise `KeccakModel S` (Verify/Spec/KeccakModel.lean), in
+the style of the two EVM verifiers that model keccak256 the same way.
+
+## Prior art
+
+**hevm** represents `SHA3` as the uninterpreted term constructor `Keccak :: Expr Buf -> Expr EWord`:
+the hash of a symbolic buffer is a term, never a computed value, and the SMT encoding declares
+`keccak` as an uninterpreted function. To make storage reasoning work it adds, for every pair of
+keccak terms `(b1, b2)` occurring in a query, the quantifier-free assertion `b1 != b2 ->
+keccak(b1) != keccak(b2)` (pairwise injectivity, src/EVM/Keccak.hs), plus lower bounds on the
+results. Because the function is otherwise free, a counterexample may use hash values the real
+keccak256 never produces (hevm documents these as possible false positives:
+https://hevm.dev/completeness-and-false-positives.html; Dxo et al., "hevm, a Fast Symbolic Execution
+Framework for EVM Bytecode", CAV 2024).
+
+**Certora** models keccak256 "as an arbitrary function that is injective with large gaps"
+(https://docs.certora.com/en/latest/docs/prover/approx/hashing.html): distinct inputs hash far
+apart, so `keccak(a) + i != keccak(b) + j` for the offsets of array elements, and the results avoid
+the reserved slots 0 to 10000 and the large constants of the code, so no hash is a slot of a static
+state variable.
+
+## The model
+
+```lean
+structure KeccakModel (S : Preimages) : Prop where
+  reserved : ∀ x, S x → 2 ^ 128 ≤ keccakWord x
+  room : ∀ x, S x → keccakWord x + 2 ^ 64 ≤ 2 ^ 256
+  gap : ∀ x y, S x → S y → x ≠ y →
+    keccakWord x + 2 ^ 64 ≤ keccakWord y ∨ keccakWord y + 2 ^ 64 ≤ keccakWord x
+```
+
+| Field / lemma | Meaning | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| `KeccakModel.inj` (from `gap`) | distinct preimages of `S` hash to distinct words | hevm's pairwise injectivity |
+| `gap` | distinct preimages hash at least `2^64` apart | Certora's large gaps |
+| `reserved` | every image is at least `2^128` (so above Certora's reserved 0..10000, `not_reserved`) | Certora's reserved slots |
+| `room` | every image is at most `2^256 - 2^64`: an offset `i < 2^64` does not wrap | Certora's offsets |
+| `offset_ne`, `offset_inj`, `offset_ne_small` | `H x + i` never equals `H y + j` (`x != y`), nor `H x + j` (`i != j`), nor a slot `c < 2^128` | the slot separation storage proofs need |
+
+`keccakWord` is the real keccak256 (EvmYul's sponge, the function SolidCore and EthLib both run), so
+a theorem under `KeccakModel S` is about the real EVM. The model is *uninterpreted* in the sense of
+hevm and Certora: the storage proofs never evaluate it on a symbolic slot. The tree tactics
+(`tree_meets_map`, `tree_meets_map2`) derive the facts they need from the premise and then
+`generalize solHash = H`, so the rest of the proof is about an arbitrary function `H` with those
+facts. It is a premise, never an axiom: the axiom audit still admits only `propext`,
+`Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.
+
+## Which preimage sets
+
+A model on every input is false (`not_keccakModel_univ`). The set `S` names the slots a contract's
+proofs use:
+
+* `mapSlots ms`: `m[a]` for every address `a` and every mapping slot `m ∈ ms`. Token uses
+  `KeccakModel (mapSlots [0])` (`balanceOf`).
+* `nestedSlots ms ns K`: `m[a]` for `m ∈ ms ++ ns`, and the nested slots `n[b][a]` for `n ∈ ns` and
+  all addresses `a`, `b` **of which one is in the finite list K**. UniswapV2ERC20 uses
+  `KeccakModel (nestedSlots [1, 4] [2] [0, 8192])`: `balanceOf` (1), `nonces` (4), `allowance` (2), with
+  the owner or the spender of every allowance slot the specs touch being `address(0)` (the
+  invariant `allowance[address(0)][s] == 0`) or the stage's caller `0x2000` (approve, transferFrom).
+
+The restriction to K is necessary. Over all pairs of addresses the nested set has `2^320`
+preimages, and the model would make `(a, c) ↦ keccak(a . keccak(c . n))` injective into `2^256`
+words. `not_nestedSlotsSeparated` refutes that by counting (Mathlib's `Fintype.card_le_of_injective`).
+This also refutes the earlier premise `NestedSlotsSeparated [1, 4] [2]` of the UniswapV2ERC20
+statements (`not_nestedSlotsSeparated_erc20`), so those statements were vacuous. `nestedSlots ms ns K`
+has about `(|ms| + |ns| + 2|ns||K|) · 2^160` preimages, which fit, and `keccakModel_mapping`
+checks the model on concrete mapping preimages in the kernel (non-vacuity on real values).
+
+### What remains assumed
+
+`KeccakModel` over a set of all addresses (`mapSlots`, `nestedSlots`) is not refutable in Lean and
+no counterexample is known, but it is a strong assumption. A random function on `2^160` inputs
+into `2^256` words is expected to have about `2^63` colliding pairs, and many more pairs closer than
+`2^64`, so these universal sets are expected to contain collisions of the real keccak256 that nobody
+can find. hevm's justification is per query: it assumes injectivity only of the finitely many hashes
+of one execution, which the real keccak256 satisfies except with negligible probability. The
+matching Lean form is a per-call premise, `KeccakModel (preimagesOf call)` inside the statement's
+quantifier over valid calls (as `TrustedBase.Hyps.keccakSeparated call` already does), with the
+specification's universally quantified slots asking only that the call's own writes avoid them.
+That form needs the generated statements to carry the premise in the postcondition rather than as
+a top-level hypothesis, and is not done here.
+
+## Derived premises
+
+| Earlier premise | Now |
+|---|---|
+| Token `HashInj` | `hashInj_of_model : KeccakModel (mapSlots [0]) → HashInj` (Contracts/Token/VC/Transfer.lean) |
+| `SlotsSeparated m` | `KeccakModel.slotsSeparated` |
+| `MapSlotsSeparated ms` | `KeccakModel.mapSlotsSeparated` |
+| `NestedSlotsSeparated ms ns` | refuted (`not_nestedSlotsSeparated`); replaced by `KeccakModel (nestedSlots ms ns K)` with `nmapK_ge_n`, `nmapK_inj_ln`, `nmapK_inj_nn` |
+
+The published statements take `KeccakModel` as their only keccak256 premise:
+`Contracts.Token.spec_holds_of_bytecode`, `Certified.verify_token.Shape.published` (and the
+statement solar's driver builds from Certified/verify_token/shape.json), and the UniswapV2ERC20
+statements (`EndToEnd.published`, `EndToEndAll.published`, `EndToEndTFSpec.published_tf`,
+`specs_hold_in`, and the `_holds` theorems solar's tools/certify/spec_connect.py generates).
+
+## Negative controls
+
+* `not_keccakModel_univ`: the model on every input is false.
+* `not_nestedSlotsSeparated`, `not_nestedSlotsSeparated_erc20`, `not_keccakModel_nested_all`: the nested
+  model over all pairs of addresses is false by counting.
+* `no_slot_collision`, `no_nested_collision`: a specification that needs two modeled slots to
+  coincide (two distinct addresses sharing a `balanceOf` slot, an allowance slot equal to a balance
+  slot) is refuted under the model, so it cannot be proved from it (the model itself is satisfiable
+  on concrete preimages, `keccakModel_mapping`).
+* solar's driver: `check_final` refuses a statement with the refuted premise
+  `NestedSlotsSeparated`, and `final.py` refuses a shape.json `env` that states keccak256 as
+  `HashInj`, `NestedSlotsSeparated`, `MapSlotsSeparated`, `SlotsSeparated` or `KeccakSeparated`,
+  or names the model twice.
+
+## In the certify driver
+
+solar's `tools/certify/check_final.lean` reads the claim's leading premises from the compiled
+statement and prints each as a `PREMISE` line, and the keccak256 model also as
+`KECCAK_MODEL SolidCore.Spec.KeccakModel S`. `scripts/certify` records them
+(`statuses.premises`, `statuses.keccak_model`) and prints `premises:` and `keccak:` lines beside the
+statuses. `spec_connect.py` emits `(hk : KeccakModel (nestedSlots ms ns [0, 8192]))` or
+`(hk : KeccakModel (mapSlots ms))` for the functions it connects.
+
+## Migrating a proof
+
+Replace `(hsep : NestedSlotsSeparated ms ns)` by `(hk : KeccakModel (nestedSlots ms ns [0, 8192]))`
+and pass `hk` where `hsep` went; `tree_meets_map2` and `tree_meets_map2_on` take it unchanged. Replace
+`(hsep : MapSlotsSeparated ms)` by `(hk : KeccakModel (mapSlots ms))` and pass
+`KeccakModel.mapSlotsSeparated hk` to `tree_meets_map`. A nested slot whose two keys are both
+outside K is not covered: its fact is left out, and a proof that needs it fails.
